#
# Findings this project has looked at and decided against acting on. Each needs a
# reason; "noisy" is not one. Nothing here suppresses a vulnerability — only
# misconfiguration rules whose advice contradicts a decision already recorded.

# DS-0026 — "Add HEALTHCHECK instruction in your Dockerfile".
#
# Every service in this deployment HAS a health check, and it is declared in
# `deploy/services.yaml` beside its interval, its start period and the group that
# waits on it. That file is the single source of truth for the topology
# (CLAUDE.md, "Where things go"), and the Quadlet units and compose.yaml are
# generated from it — so a HEALTHCHECK baked into a Dockerfile would be the same
# fact stated twice, in a place the generator does not read and the drift check
# cannot compare. `REQ-CON-015` is the rule against exactly that.
#
# The trade is real and is accepted: an image run outside this deployment has no
# health check of its own. It also has no network, no secrets and no database, so
# it is not a configuration anybody runs.
DS-0026
